{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A SAML 2.0 protocol binding (SAML Bindings §3). The response binding for Web Browser SSO is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"always ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::HttpPost"},{"type":"text","text":"], but the enum keeps both because SP metadata carries both, and an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"slo_url"},{"type":"text","text":" may use either."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SamlBinding","kind":"identifier"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"open"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" enum. A value this SDK’s copy of the spec does not list decodes to ","type":"text"},{"code":".unknown","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rather than failing the response it arrived in (CONTRACT.md §27.11 rule 1). Throwing there","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fails the WHOLE response, so one field of one record would take down the page it was on,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"including the records the caller did ask for.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is never read as one of the KNOWN cases: reading a new value as whichever case happens to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be first turns a new server state into a wrong one, and on this surface these values gate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"access. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"type":"text","text":"’s own raw value is the empty string, which no server value is, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"type":"text","text":" is never written: "},{"type":"c